.TH "sysforge" "1" "2026\-07\-21"
.PP
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
sysforge \- build and maintenance suite and system bootstrapper for Arch Linux
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBsysforge\fR [\fB\-v\fR.\&.\&.\&] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIARGS\fR.\&.\&.\&]
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
SysForge builds AUR and custom packages with rule\-matched compiler\-flag
profiles: every package is built with the optimization flags its matching
profile resolves (\-march=native, LTO, linker choice, caches), while pacman
remains the owner of the package database.\& Build metadata — versions, the
resolved flags, toolchain identity, source provenance, and the reviewed
source commit — is recorded per package in build_state.\&toml and drives
update, drift detection, and diagnostics.\&
.PP
\fBsysforge update\fR is the steady\-state entry point: it walks the live install
set (all foreign packages, plus repo packages selected by overrides or
repo_mode = "build_from_source"), syncs sources through a rate\-limited scheduler,
compares versions, reports toolchain\-variant and compiler\-flag drift, and
rebuilds what changed.\& Before any changed source is built, the PKGBUILD
review gate presents the full source\-tree diff since the last accepted
build for approval (see \fB\-\-no\-review\fR).\& Builds run through a managed
makepkg invocation with dependencies pre\-installed, per\-package logs, build
failure diagnosis with deterministic auto\-repair for known failure modes,
and a single bulk install at the end.\&
.PP
\fBsysforge run\fR executes pipeline stages: the bootstrap stages that take a
fresh Arch ISO environment to a configured system (install via archinstall,
hardware detection, configure), and the repeatable stages (toolchain,
kernel, packages, reconfigure) that build an optionally PGO\-optimized LLVM
toolchain and a custom kernel under boot\-safety gates.\&
.PP
\fBsysforge doctor\fR is the read\-only health surface: package depends + ABI
linkage walks plus system\-state axes (hardware, toolchain, pacman db,
state, boot, storage, services, graphics).\&
.PP
Install\-bearing commands write a stage sentinel before mutating the system;
an interrupted run is detected on the next invocation and offers a recorded
recovery command.\&
.PP
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.PP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
.RS 4
Increase verbosity.\& Default shows errors only; \-v adds warnings, \-vv
informational messages, \-vvv debug output (repeatable, position
independent).\& The default level (when no flag is passed) can be raised
via the \fB[log] verbosity\fR key in \fIsysforge.\&toml\fR; a CLI flag always wins.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-quiet\fR
.RS 4
Suppress all non\-error output (verbosity 0), overriding both \fB\-v\fR and
the \fB[log] verbosity\fR config default.\& File logs still record every
level.\& Distinct from \fBdoctor\fR'\&s local \fB\-\-quiet\fR (which suppresses clean
diagnostic lines).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
.RS 4
Print the sysforge version and exit.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-py\-profile\fR
.RS 4
Run the verb under the Python profiler (cProfile) and print the top
functions by cumulative time to stderr at exit.\& Position independent.\&
Profiles sysforge'\&s own runtime only; subprocess work (makepkg, pacman,
git) appears as wait time — use \fB\-\-timings\fR for wall\-clock phase costs.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-py\-profile\-out\fR \fIFILE\fR
.RS 4
Write raw cProfile stats to \fIFILE\fR for later analysis (pstats,
snakeviz).\& Implies \fB\-\-py\-profile\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-timings\fR
.RS 4
Print a wall\-clock phase timing report (source sync, version check,
drift detection, per\-package builds, install, pacman \-Syu) after
\fBbuild\fR and \fBupdate\fR runs.\& Without the flag the report is still
written to the log at info level.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-color\fR \fIauto\fR|\fIalways\fR|\fInever\fR
.RS 4
Colorize output.\& \fIauto\fR (the default) colours when writing to a
terminal and honours the \fBNO_COLOR\fR and \fBFORCE_COLOR\fR environment
variables; \fIalways\fR forces colour on (useful when piping into a pager
such as \fBless \-R\fR); \fInever\fR disables it.\& Overrides the \fB[ui] color\fR
key in \fIsysforge.\&toml\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-throttle\fR
.RS 4
Ignore the configured build throttle (\fBnice\fR/\fBionice\fR/\fBcpu_quota\fR/\fBjobs\fR
from \fB[build]\fR) for this run, building at normal unthrottled priority.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-turbo\fR
.RS 4
Run the build at \fIhigher\fR than default priority: negative niceness and
best\-effort IO, with no CPU ceiling or job cap.\& Stronger than
\fB\-\-no\-throttle\fR.\& Lowering niceness may require privilege; when the kernel
refuses, the build runs at the current priority (best\-effort, never fatal).\&
.PP
.RE
.SH COMMANDS
.PP
.SS build
.PP
\fBsysforge build\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIPKGBUILD.\&.\&.\&\fR
.PP
Build a package from a PKGBUILD.\&
.PP
\fBPKGBUILD\fR
.RS 4
One or more packages to build (path, directory, or bare package name).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-makepkg\fR, \fB\-m\fR \fIFLAGS\fR
.RS 4
Additional makepkg flags, appended after profile makepkg_flags.\& Usually optional: bare makepkg short flags are forwarded implicitly (sysforge build PKGBUILD \-sfc works without \-m).\& \-m is only needed for makepkg long flags (e.\&g.\& \-\-skippgpcheck), flags that take a value (\-p, \-D), or flags sysforge claims for itself (\-h, \-V).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-interactive\fR
.RS 4
Strip \-\-noconfirm from profile makepkg_flags and hand stdout/stderr to makepkg'\&s terminal so pacman conflict prompts and other unbuffered interactive output appear immediately (disables line\-based output classification while set).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-persist\-log\fR
.RS 4
Keep the per\-package log file after a successful build.\& Also settable via [build] persist_log = true in packages.\&toml.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-pkg\-log\fR
.RS 4
Disable the per\-package log file.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-log\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR
.RS 4
Directory for the per\-package log file (default: alongside the PKGBUILD).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-profile\-conf\fR \fIFILE\fR
.RS 4
Path to a profiles.\&toml to use instead of the default.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-cc\fR \fICOMPILER\fR
.RS 4
Override CC (C compiler) for this build, e.\&g.\& \-\-cc clang.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-cxx\fR \fICOMPILER\fR
.RS 4
Override CXX (C++ compiler) for this build, e.\&g.\& \-\-cxx clang++.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-ld\fR \fILINKER\fR
.RS 4
Override linker for this build, e.\&g.\& \-\-ld lld.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-cache\-report\fR
.RS 4
Print a structured cache summary (ccache/sccache hit rates) after the build.\& Also settable via [build] cache_report = true in packages.\&toml.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-abi\-check\fR
.RS 4
Run a post\-build ABI compatibility check on built shared libraries.\& Also settable via [build] abi_check = true in packages.\&toml.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-update\fR
.RS 4
Skip git pull \-\-rebase before building.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-cleansrc\fR
.RS 4
Purge the package src dir and re\-clone before building.\& Refuses (per package) if the existing clone has uncommitted changes, ahead\-of\-upstream commits, or no upstream tracking branch.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-cleansrc\-force\fR
.RS 4
Like \-\-cleansrc but bypasses the dirty/diverged guard and overwrites the local tree unconditionally.\& Use when the upstream rewrote history (e.\&g.\& Arch packaging repos force\-push every release) and the local commits have no value to preserve.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-llvm\-preflight\fR
.RS 4
Suppress the LLVM source pre\-flight summary.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-review\fR
.RS 4
Skip the PKGBUILD review gate (full source\-tree diff prompt for packages whose source changed since the last accepted build).\& Also configurable via [build] review = false in packages.\&toml.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-force\fR
.RS 4
Unconditionally build all arguments from source for this run only, including repo packages not yet opted in.\& Never prompts for or modifies packages.\&toml opt\-in keys.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-pgo\fR \fIPGO_MODE\fR
.RS 4
Mesa instrumentation PGO (LLVM toolchain only).\& \-\-pgo=record builds+installs an instrumented mesa that writes profile data to the sysforge store as you run graphics workloads; \-\-pgo=use merges the collected profiles and rebuilds an optimized mesa\-sysforge (conflicts/replaces stock mesa).\& No\-op for non\-mesa targets.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR
.RS 4
Override state directory for build_state.\&toml.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBConfiguration:\fR profiles.\&toml, packages.\&toml ([build]), sysforge.\&toml ([git])
.PP
\fBEnvironment:\fR $SYSFORGE_CONFIG_DIR, $SYSFORGE_STATE_DIR, $PAGER (review diffs)
.PP
.SS update
.PP
\fBsysforge update\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fI[PKG.\&.\&.\&]\fR
.PP
Check for and rebuild outdated sysforge\-managed packages.\&
.PP
\fBPKG\fR
.RS 4
Limit update to these package names (default: all sysforge\-managed packages).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
.RS 4
Show what would be rebuilt without doing it.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-devel\fR
.RS 4
Resolve and rebuild VCS packages (\-git, \-svn, \-hg, \-bzr) whose upstream HEAD has advanced past the installed version.\& Resolution runs makepkg \-\-nobuild per VCS package; up\-to\-date packages are skipped, not rebuilt.\& Per\-package upstream commits recorded in build_state are reused on subsequent runs to short\-circuit the resolve via git ls\-remote.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-offline\fR
.RS 4
No network: skip git pulls, clones, and AUR RPC.\& Pure local version check.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-install\-only\fR
.RS 4
Skip rebuild; install only those locally\-built artifacts in PKGDEST that are newer than the installed version.\& Implies \-\-offline.\& Mutually exclusive with \-\-makepkg, \-\-no\-cleanbuild, \-\-cleansrc, \-\-cleansrc\-force, \-\-interactive, and \-\-cache\-report.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-packages\fR \fIFILE\fR
.RS 4
Path to packages.\&toml for override rules (default: /etc/sysforge/packages.\&toml; override the dir with $SYSFORGE_CONFIG_DIR).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR
.RS 4
Override state directory.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-profile\-conf\fR \fIFILE\fR
.RS 4
Path to a profiles.\&toml to use instead of the default.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-cache\-report\fR
.RS 4
Print a structured cache summary after the run.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-pkg\-log\fR
.RS 4
Disable per\-package log files.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-persist\-log\fR
.RS 4
Keep log files after successful completion.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-log\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR
.RS 4
Directory for per\-package log files.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-makepkg\fR, \fB\-m\fR \fIFLAGS\fR
.RS 4
Extra flags passed verbatim to makepkg.\& Usually optional: bare makepkg short flags are forwarded implicitly (sysforge update \-f works without \-m).\& \-m is only needed for makepkg long flags (e.\&g.\& \-\-skippgpcheck), flags that take a value (\-p, \-D), or flags sysforge claims for itself (\-h, \-V).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-interactive\fR
.RS 4
Pause on build failures to allow manual correction (default: log failure and continue).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-cleanbuild\fR
.RS 4
Skip the automatic \-\-cleanbuild (\-C) added for update runs.\& Useful when packages are already built and you only need to re\-run the install step.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-cleansrc\fR
.RS 4
Purge each package'\&s src dir and re\-clone before building.\& Per\-package fatal if the clone has uncommitted changes, ahead\-of\-upstream commits, or no upstream — that package is reported failed and the run continues.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-cleansrc\-force\fR
.RS 4
Like \-\-cleansrc but bypasses the dirty/diverged guard and overwrites every local tree unconditionally.\& Use when the upstream rewrote history (e.\&g.\& Arch packaging repos force\-push every release) and local commits have no value to preserve.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-llvm\-preflight\fR
.RS 4
Suppress the LLVM source pre\-flight summary.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-review\fR
.RS 4
Prompt to review the full source\-tree diff for packages whose source changed since the last accepted build.\& By default update auto\-accepts changes with a logged notice so batch runs stay unattended; use `sysforge build` or this flag to inspect diffs.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-review\fR
.RS 4
Skip the PKGBUILD review gate entirely (no auto\-accept notices).\& Also configurable via [build] review = false in packages.\&toml.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-toolchain\-preflight\fR
.RS 4
Skip the toolchain pre\-flight (rust/cmake/meson availability + lib32 cross targets) that normally runs before the build loop.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-include\-stage\-owned\fR
.RS 4
Include packages owned by a pipeline stage (e.\&g.\& the kernel stage'\&s `linux\-sysforge`).\& Skipped by default; the owning stage (`sysforge run kernel`) is the canonical update path.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-explain\-drift\fR
.RS 4
List drifted packages and exit, across both axes: toolchain drift (recorded toolchain_variant differs from the active gcc / stock_llvm / pgo_llvm) and flag drift (profiled packages whose flags now resolve differently than when built, with a per\-key diff).\& Informational; no source sync, no rebuild.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-rebuild\-on\-toolchain\-drift\fR
.RS 4
Treat toolchain\-variant drift as an upgrade trigger: packages built under a different toolchain than is active now are added to the rebuild queue.\& Off by default — drift is reported but not acted on, since most C/C++ packages don'\&t measurably benefit from a re\-stamp.\& Also settable via [update] rebuild_on_toolchain_drift = true in sysforge.\&toml.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-rebuild\-on\-flag\-drift\fR
.RS 4
Treat flag drift as an upgrade trigger: profiled packages whose flags now resolve differently than when built are added to the rebuild queue.\& Off by default — flag drift is reported but not acted on, since one profile edit can drift every profiled package.\& Also settable via [update] rebuild_on_flag_drift = true in sysforge.\&toml.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-rebuild\-on\-drift\fR
.RS 4
Umbrella for both \-\-rebuild\-on\-toolchain\-drift and \-\-rebuild\-on\-flag\-drift: rebuild anything that has drifted.\& Also settable via [update] rebuild_on_drift = true in sysforge.\&toml.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBConfiguration:\fR profiles.\&toml, packages.\&toml, sysforge.\&toml ([git], failure_handling)
.PP
\fBEnvironment:\fR $SYSFORGE_CONFIG_DIR, $SYSFORGE_STATE_DIR, $PAGER (review diffs)
.PP
.SS fetch
.PP
\fBsysforge fetch\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIPKG.\&.\&.\&\fR
.PP
Download PKGBUILD(s) into pkgbuild_src_dir without building.\&
.PP
\fBPKG\fR
.RS 4
One or more package names to download.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-update\fR
.RS 4
Skip git pull \-\-rebase for packages that are already cloned.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-cleansrc\fR
.RS 4
Purge each package'\&s src dir and re\-clone.\& Refuses (per package) if the existing clone has uncommitted changes, ahead\-of\-upstream commits, or no upstream tracking branch.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-cleansrc\-force\fR
.RS 4
Like \-\-cleansrc but bypasses the dirty/diverged guard and overwrites the local tree unconditionally.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-llvm\-preflight\fR
.RS 4
Suppress the LLVM source pre\-flight summary.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-profile\-conf\fR \fIFILE\fR
.RS 4
Path to a profiles.\&toml to use instead of the default.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBConfiguration:\fR profiles.\&toml ([paths]), sysforge.\&toml ([git])
.PP
\fBEnvironment:\fR $SYSFORGE_CONFIG_DIR
.PP
.SS search
.PP
\fBsysforge search\fR \fITERM\fR
.PP
Search installed, repo, and AUR packages for a term.\&
.PP
\fBTERM\fR
.RS 4
search term (name + description)
.PP
.RE
.SS doctor
.PP
\fBsysforge doctor\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fI[PKG.\&.\&.\&]\fR
.PP
Diagnose sysforge\-managed system health (linkage, toolchain, hardware, graphics, pacman, state, boot, services, audio, network).\&
.PP
\fBPKG\fR
.RS 4
One or more installed package names to verify (package depends + ABI linkage walk).\& With no PKG and no axis flag, bare `doctor` runs every system\-state axis — the fast full sweep.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-graphics\fR
.RS 4
Expand to the graphics stack (mesa, vulkan, libglvnd, wayland, libdrm, libva, libvdpau, egl\-wayland, xwayland, gamescope, plus per\-vendor drivers from the hardware overlay'\&s gpu_vendors) AND run system\-state probes (nvidia\-drm modeset, driver version skew, Wayland explicit\-sync protocol, Steam GPU accel, session type).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-gfxperf\fR
.RS 4
Advisory graphics\-performance sweep (stutter/tearing/frame\-drop contributors: video\-decode path, GPU power/clocks, CPU governor, frame pacing, thermal).\& Opt\-in; never fails.\& Combine with \-\-graphics for the full graphics picture.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-hardware\fR
.RS 4
Run system\-state hardware probes: inventory all PCI/USB devices, flag any present device with no kernel driver bound, and audit the running kernel'\&s .\&config for boot\-critical / device\-driver gaps (the missing\-driver class of bug).\& Usable on its own (no PKG).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-toolchain\fR
.RS 4
Check that the configured toolchain matches what'\&s installed: when toolchain.\&toml requests a custom LLVM toolchain (compiler = llvm, optionally PGO) but stock repo LLVM is installed — or the PGO profdata is version\-skewed — report it.\& Usable on its own (no PKG).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-cache\fR
.RS 4
Check compile\-cache readiness *before* a build relies on it: whether ccache/sccache are installed, their cache dir is writable, and a non\-zero size cap is set.\& Absence is informational, not a failure.\& Distinct from build verbs'\& \-\-cache\-report, which measures per\-package hit rates *after* a build.\& Usable on its own (no PKG).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-pacman\fR
.RS 4
Check local package\-database integrity (read\-only, never syncs): `pacman \-Dk` dependency consistency, a stale db.\&lck, unmerged .\&pacnew/.\&pacsave config files under /etc, and orphan packages.\& Usable on its own (no PKG).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-state\fR
.RS 4
Check sysforge'\&s own state integrity: recorded build failures, an interrupted stage sentinel from a prior run, and build_state drift vs the live pacman database.\& Read\-only (does not recover).\& Usable on its own (no PKG).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-boot\fR
.RS 4
Check running\-system boot readiness (reusing the kernel stage'\&s safety primitives): per\-kernel boot artifacts (vmlinuz + initramfs + boot entry), a recovery fallback kernel, /boot space, and DKMS modules for the running kernel.\& Usable on its own (no PKG).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-restart\fR
.RS 4
Check whether upgraded packages have actually taken effect: scans running processes for files replaced on disk (a `(deleted)` mapping) and reports whether the fix is a unit restart, a re\-login, or a reboot.\& Read\-only; never escalates, so coverage of other users'\& processes is reported as incomplete rather than prompting.\& Usable on its own (no PKG).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-storage\fR
.RS 4
Check storage/filesystem health: free space on the build dir (warns under [doctor] disk_low_gb) and /etc/fstab integrity (entries whose UUID/label/device no longer resolves).\& Read\-only; never mounts.\& Usable on its own (no PKG).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-services\fR
.RS 4
Check live service/driver runtime health: failed systemd units (`systemctl \-\-failed`), firmware a driver requested but could not load this boot, and error\-priority journal lines this boot.\& Usable on its own (no PKG).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-audio\fR
.RS 4
Check live PipeWire/WirePlumber sound\-stack health: failed audio user services (`systemctl \-\-user \-\-failed`) and a vanished output sink (only the dummy auto_null device present).\& User\-scoped, so it degrades to clean under sudo.\& Usable on its own (no PKG).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-network\fR
.RS 4
Check network/connectivity configuration: no default route, connection\-manager ownership conflicts (more than one of NetworkManager/systemd\-networkd/dhcpcd/… enabled), and a DNS provisioner conflict (systemd\-resolved active but /etc/resolv.\&conf is a static override).\& Read\-only; no live network calls.\& Usable on its own (no PKG).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-integrity\fR
.RS 4
Verify package\-owned files against alpm'\&s recorded mtree via `pacman \-Qkk`: files an admin or a misbehaving install script altered or removed outside a pacman transaction.\& Opt\-in (excluded from the bare/full sweep because a whole\-system scan re\-hashes every packaged file); scope it with `doctor \-\-integrity PKG…`.\& Read\-only; never restores.\& Usable on its own (no PKG).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-all\fR
.RS 4
Run every system\-state axis AND the full per\-package walk over every installed package — foreign and non\-foreign (pacman \-Q).\& The exhaustive '\&is anything broken anywhere'\& sweep.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-repo\fR
.RS 4
Walk every non\-foreign (native repo) package.\& Package walk only, no system axes; narrower than \-\-all.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-shallow\fR
.RS 4
Do not recurse into transitive dependencies of each target.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-quiet\fR, \fB\-q\fR
.RS 4
Suppress clean lines; print only packages with issues.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-suggest\fR, \fB\-s\fR
.RS 4
For each unsatisfied soname, look up candidate packages via `pacman \-Fq`.\& Findings split into '\&install candidates'\& (missing from disk — install the package), '\&rebuild candidates'\& (installed; rebuild against the current system), and '\&ABI\-drift candidates'\& (present but one of their versioned symbols no longer resolves — rebuild or upgrade, not reinstall).\& Requires a synced files db (`sudo pacman \-Fy`).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-apply\fR
.RS 4
Hand the rebuild candidates from \-\-suggest off to `sysforge update` and rebuild them.\& Implies \-\-suggest.\& Drift\-rebuild only in v1.\&x — install candidates are printed but not invoked.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-confirm\fR
.RS 4
Skip the y/N prompt before \-\-apply rebuilds.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
.RS 4
Report what \-\-apply would rebuild without invoking the build.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBConfiguration:\fR profiles.\&toml; toolchain.\&toml and kernel.\&toml on their axes
.PP
\fBEnvironment:\fR $SYSFORGE_CONFIG_DIR, $SYSFORGE_STATE_DIR
.PP
